[[:db/retract 17592186191092 :answer-field/choices 17592186191093] [:db/retract 17592186191092 :answer-field/choices 17592186191094] [:db/retract 17592186191092 :answer-field/choices 17592186191095] [:db/retract 17592186191092 :answer-field/choices 17592186191096] [:db/retract 17592186191092 :answer-field/choices 17592186191097] {:db/id 17592186192799 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0a61b26d-5077-52d9-9883-5f2b02dfb768" "question-64c12c20-f4ed-568b-9dbd-aefd4fca5ee6" "question-d6e58c8d-9f78-5f4d-ae53-f347e7b01f68" "question-cb9c4cb7-5063-5801-b2b1-37e6379336d1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192523 :question/problem "Let $X_1, X_2, X_3$ be I.I.D. random variables with probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x; \\theta) = (\\theta+1) x^{-\\theta-2}, \\qquad x \\geq 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\theta$ is an unknown parameter. Find the likelihood function of the sample $2.0, \\, 4.5, \\,5.1 .$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_{n}$ are independent and identically distributed continuous random variables with probability density function $f(x; \\theta),$ where $\\theta$ is an unknown parameter, then the likelihood function of a random sample $x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n$ is\n\n$$\nL(\\theta) = P(X_1=x_1, X_2=x_2, \\ldots , X_n = x_n) = \\displaystyle\\prod_{i=1}^n f(x_i;\\,\\theta).\n$$\n\n$$\nf(x; \\theta) = (\\theta+1) x^{-\\theta-2}, \\qquad x \\geq 1.\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the likelihood function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & ={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}((\\theta +1){x}_{i}^{-\\theta -2}) \\\\  & =(\\theta +1)^{n}\\cdot {\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{-\\theta -2} \\\\  & =(\\theta +1)^{n}({\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})^{-\\theta -2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor our sample, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} & =2.0\\cdot 4.5\\cdot 5.1=45.9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand $n=3.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nL(\\theta) = (\\theta+1)^{3} ( 45.9 )^{-\\theta-2}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192797 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1983f891-c0ec-5f2f-97f4-aee1cde66c6b" "question-722785f1-98e4-52e2-9870-cc5147d770a3" "question-d0ac51fa-7d6b-5afa-a10b-159234b28e9a" "question-7d257a6c-5e5c-58a0-af13-fdf60799b0d8" "question-bc819016-9ccb-568a-b71d-77c2cc9598ca"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192521 :question/problem "Suppose $X_1,X_2,\\ldots,X_6$ is an I.I.D random sample with $X_i \\sim \\text{Exp}(\\theta)$ and unknown rate parameter $\\theta.$ Find the likelihood function of the sample $1.5, \\, 2.0, \\, 1.1, \\, 0.4, \\, 3.3, \\, 2.7.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_{n}$ are independent and identically distributed continuous random variables with probability density function $f(x; \\theta),$ where $\\theta$ is an unknown parameter, then the likelihood function of a random sample $x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n$ is\n\n$$\nL(\\theta) = P(X_1=x_1, X_2=x_2, \\ldots , X_n = x_n) = \\displaystyle\\prod_{i=1}^n f(x_i;\\,\\theta).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we are given a sample of $n=6$ independent exponential random variables with unknown parameter $\\theta,$ for which the probability density function is\n\n$$\nf(x; \\,\\theta) = \\theta e^{-\\theta x}, \\qquad x\\geq 0.\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the likelihood function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & ={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}\\theta {e}^{-\\theta {x}_{i}} \\\\  & =(\\theta {e}^{-\\theta {x}_{1}})\\cdot (\\theta {e}^{-\\theta {x}_{2}})⋯(\\theta {e}^{-\\theta {x}_{n}}) \\\\  & ={\\theta }^{n}\\,{e}^{-\\theta ({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+⋯+{x}_{n})} \\\\  & ={\\theta }^{n}\\,{e}^{-\\theta \\sum {x}_{i}} \\\\  & ={\\theta }^{n}\\,{e}^{-S\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\displaystyle S = \\sum\\limits_ {i=1}^n x_i.$ \n\nFor our sample, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =1.5+2.0+1.1+0.4+3.3+2.7 \\\\  & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand $n=6.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & ={\\theta }^{6}\\,{e}^{-11\\theta }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192684 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5ede7a13-53b1-5dcd-b174-1b2115493b08" "question-0b9cdfe0-b9cf-519c-9814-c1b778856085" "question-2015b9da-5691-5067-96fe-7987a1cb7888" "question-48c555e3-358d-5d44-81b1-fa7fdd197fa6" "question-2f4678d5-a087-5e11-90cc-f482d76b03ff"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192389 :question/problem "Suppose $X_1,X_2,X_3,X_4$ is an I.I.D random sample with $X_i \\sim N(\\theta, 1),$ where $\\theta$ is an unknown mean. Find the likelihood function of the sample $0.4,\\, -0.3,\\, -2.2,\\, -0.4.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_{n}$ are independent and identically distributed continuous random variables with probability density function $f(x; \\theta),$ where $\\theta$ is an unknown parameter, then the likelihood function of a random sample $x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n$ is\n\n$$\nL(\\theta) = P(X_1=x_1, X_2=x_2, \\ldots , X_n = x_n) = \\displaystyle\\prod_{i=1}^n f(x_i;\\,\\theta).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we are given a sample of $n=4$ independent normal random variables with unknown mean $\\theta$ and variance $\\sigma^2 = 1,$ for which the probability density function is\n\n$$\nf(x; \\theta) = \\dfrac{1}{\\sigma \\sqrt{2\\pi}} e^{-\\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\frac{x-\\theta}{\\sigma} \\right)^2} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\pi}} e^{-(x-\\theta)^2/2}, \\qquad x \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the likelihood function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & ={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\pi }}{e}^{-({x}_{i}-\\theta )^{2}/2}) \\\\  & =(2\\pi )^{-n/2}\\,{e}^{-\\sum ({x}_{i}-\\theta )^{2}/2} \\\\  & =(2\\pi )^{-n/2}\\,{e}^{-(\\sum {x}_{i}^{2}-2\\theta \\sum {x}_{i}+n{\\theta }^{2})/2} \\\\  & =(2\\pi )^{-n/2}\\,{e}^{-(C-2S\\theta +n{\\theta }^{2})/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\displaystyle S = \\sum\\limits_ {i=1}^n x_i$ and $\\displaystyle C = \\sum\\limits_ {i=1}^n x_i^2.$\n\nFor our sample, we have that $n=4,$ and \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =0.4+(-0.3)+(-2.2)+(-0.4) \\\\  & =-2.5 \\\\ C & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =(0.4)^{2}+(-0.3)^{2}+(-2.2)^{2}+(-0.4)^{2} \\\\  & =5.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & =(2\\pi )^{-4/2}\\,{e}^{-(5.25-2(-2.5)\\theta +4{\\theta }^{2})/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{\\pi }^{2}}\\,{e}^{-2.625\\,-\\,2.5\\theta \\,-\\,2{\\theta }^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-0a61b26d-5077-52d9-9883-5f2b02dfb768" :question/id #uuid "0a61b26d-5077-52d9-9883-5f2b02dfb768" :question/math-academy-id "q-159900" :question/problem "Let ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{18}$ be I.I.D. random variables with probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x;\\theta )=\\theta {x}^{-\\theta -1},\\,x\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\theta $ is an unknown parameter. For a particular sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{18},$ you're given that \n\n$$\n{\\prod }_{i=1}^{18}{x}_{i}=34.2.\n$$\n\nFind the likelihood function of the sample." :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ are independent and identically distributed continuous random variables with probability density function $f(x;\\theta ),$ where $\\theta $ is an unknown parameter, then the likelihood function of a random sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is\n\n$$\nL(\\theta )=P({X}_{1}={x}_{1},{X}_{2}={x}_{2},…,{X}_{n}={x}_{n})={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i};\\,\\theta ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we are given a sample of $n=18$ independent random variables with unknown parameter $\\theta ,$ for which the probability density function is\n\n$$\nf(x;\\theta )=\\theta {x}^{-\\theta -1},\\,x\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the likelihood function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & ={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}(\\theta {x}_{i}^{-\\theta -1}) \\\\  & ={\\theta }^{n}\\cdot {\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{-\\theta -1} \\\\  & ={\\theta }^{n}({\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})^{-\\theta -1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are told that ${\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}=34.2$ and $n=18.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nL(\\theta )={\\theta }^{18}(34.2)^{-\\theta -1}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b7072343-82c3-507f-9cad-e945e7d13486"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b7072343-82c3-507f-9cad-e945e7d13486" :answer-field/id #uuid "b7072343-82c3-507f-9cad-e945e7d13486" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3ca16ed7-9e4e-56eb-bd2f-6ebfc4d41e34" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dfed62d0-af8d-5410-a887-75b2dc334c9a" "answer-3ca16ed7-9e4e-56eb-bd2f-6ebfc4d41e34" "answer-704331ed-2fd4-5536-aec5-80c3089dc326" "answer-82930bd9-d015-56dc-b6b7-95c871d9fe80" "answer-e903adb3-c4f9-56c8-9655-a1a964227644"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfed62d0-af8d-5410-a887-75b2dc334c9a" :answer/id #uuid "dfed62d0-af8d-5410-a887-75b2dc334c9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\theta }^{-18}(34.2)^{\\theta -2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ca16ed7-9e4e-56eb-bd2f-6ebfc4d41e34" :answer/id #uuid "3ca16ed7-9e4e-56eb-bd2f-6ebfc4d41e34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\theta }^{18}(34.2)^{-\\theta -1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-704331ed-2fd4-5536-aec5-80c3089dc326" :answer/id #uuid "704331ed-2fd4-5536-aec5-80c3089dc326" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\theta }^{18}(34.2)^{\\theta -1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82930bd9-d015-56dc-b6b7-95c871d9fe80" :answer/id #uuid "82930bd9-d015-56dc-b6b7-95c871d9fe80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\theta }^{34.2}(18)^{-\\theta -1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e903adb3-c4f9-56c8-9655-a1a964227644" :answer/id #uuid "e903adb3-c4f9-56c8-9655-a1a964227644" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\theta }^{9}(34.2)^{-\\theta }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-64c12c20-f4ed-568b-9dbd-aefd4fca5ee6" :question/id #uuid "64c12c20-f4ed-568b-9dbd-aefd4fca5ee6" :question/math-academy-id "q-159918" :question/problem "Let ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{12}$ be I.I.D. random variables with probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x;\\theta )=(\\theta +2){x}^{-\\theta -3},\\,x\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\theta $ is an unknown parameter. For a particular sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{12},$ you're given that \n\n$$\n{\\prod }_{i=1}^{12}{x}_{i}=12.1.\n$$\n\nFind the likelihood function of the sample." :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ are independent and identically distributed continuous random variables with probability density function $f(x;\\theta ),$ where $\\theta $ is an unknown parameter, then the likelihood function of a random sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is\n\n$$\nL(\\theta )=P({X}_{1}={x}_{1},{X}_{2}={x}_{2},…,{X}_{n}={x}_{n})={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i};\\,\\theta ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we are given a sample of $n=12$ independent random variables with unknown parameter $\\theta ,$ for which the probability density function is\n\n$$\nf(x;\\theta )=(\\theta +2){x}^{-\\theta -3},\\,x\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the likelihood function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & ={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}((\\theta +2){x}_{i}^{-\\theta -3}) \\\\  & =(\\theta +2)^{n}\\cdot {\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{-\\theta -3} \\\\  & =(\\theta +2)^{n}({\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})^{-\\theta -3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are told that ${\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}=12.1$ and $n=12.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nL(\\theta )=(\\theta +2)^{12}(12.1)^{-\\theta -3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3f9e6a32-13a9-57bb-b2e7-4364b34f9b73"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3f9e6a32-13a9-57bb-b2e7-4364b34f9b73" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f9e6a32-13a9-57bb-b2e7-4364b34f9b73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8e6b4048-d8d3-5ef8-bf0c-70f04f6c23d8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-20cfd1ac-3d62-5228-8c42-0e20ad31845d" "answer-33c45630-6324-596e-b0b8-8a83b54f9dee" "answer-74738b3f-0d08-536c-91bd-808ed0f7492e" "answer-8e6b4048-d8d3-5ef8-bf0c-70f04f6c23d8" "answer-6e498b97-1a1d-57c3-b809-f7ea65d1e7a2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20cfd1ac-3d62-5228-8c42-0e20ad31845d" :answer/id #uuid "20cfd1ac-3d62-5228-8c42-0e20ad31845d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\theta +1)^{12}(12.1)^{-\\theta -4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33c45630-6324-596e-b0b8-8a83b54f9dee" :answer/id #uuid "33c45630-6324-596e-b0b8-8a83b54f9dee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\theta +2)^{12.1}(12)^{-\\theta -2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74738b3f-0d08-536c-91bd-808ed0f7492e" :answer/id #uuid "74738b3f-0d08-536c-91bd-808ed0f7492e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\theta +2)^{12.1}(12)^{-\\theta -3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e6b4048-d8d3-5ef8-bf0c-70f04f6c23d8" :answer/id #uuid "8e6b4048-d8d3-5ef8-bf0c-70f04f6c23d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\theta +2)^{12}(12.1)^{-\\theta -3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e498b97-1a1d-57c3-b809-f7ea65d1e7a2" :answer/id #uuid "6e498b97-1a1d-57c3-b809-f7ea65d1e7a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\theta +4)^{12}(12.1)^{-\\theta -2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d6e58c8d-9f78-5f4d-ae53-f347e7b01f68" :question/id #uuid "d6e58c8d-9f78-5f4d-ae53-f347e7b01f68" :question/math-academy-id "q-159923" :question/problem "Let ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},{X}_{3}$ be I.I.D. random variables with probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x;\\theta )=(\\theta +2){x}^{-\\theta -3},\\,x\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\theta $ is an unknown parameter. Find the likelihood function of the sample $1.4,\\,2.2,\\,2.5.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ are independent and identically distributed continuous random variables with probability density function $f(x;\\theta ),$ where $\\theta $ is an unknown parameter, then the likelihood function of a random sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is\n\n$$\nL(\\theta )=P({X}_{1}={x}_{1},{X}_{2}={x}_{2},…,{X}_{n}={x}_{n})={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i};\\,\\theta ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we are given a sample of $n=3$ independent random variables with unknown parameter $\\theta ,$ for which the probability density function is\n\n$$\nf(x;\\theta )=(\\theta +2){x}^{-\\theta -3},\\,x\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the likelihood function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & ={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}((\\theta +2){x}_{i}^{-\\theta -3}) \\\\  & =(\\theta +2)^{n}\\cdot {\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{-\\theta -3} \\\\  & =(\\theta +2)^{n}({\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})^{-\\theta -3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor our sample, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} & =1.4\\cdot 2.2\\cdot 2.5=7.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand $n=3.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nL(\\theta )=(\\theta +2)^{3}(7.7)^{-\\theta -3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-318e1b68-556e-56da-a5bf-0363656b0f61"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-318e1b68-556e-56da-a5bf-0363656b0f61" :answer-field/id #uuid "318e1b68-556e-56da-a5bf-0363656b0f61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8d9403b5-aafb-5d53-aa6d-0e5daf290a1a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8e460f54-8212-5400-aa16-c056c7b454f6" "answer-9f3d6e63-005e-5287-8d47-4bdb79a1a681" "answer-8d9403b5-aafb-5d53-aa6d-0e5daf290a1a" "answer-9b6284b9-9a9f-5ee1-920b-8bb95737b84a" "answer-492a6c1b-401b-53e4-ba39-5675e2455008"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e460f54-8212-5400-aa16-c056c7b454f6" :answer/id #uuid "8e460f54-8212-5400-aa16-c056c7b454f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\theta +2)^{3}(6.1)^{-\\theta +3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f3d6e63-005e-5287-8d47-4bdb79a1a681" :answer/id #uuid "9f3d6e63-005e-5287-8d47-4bdb79a1a681" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\theta +2)^{3}(6.1)^{-\\theta -3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d9403b5-aafb-5d53-aa6d-0e5daf290a1a" :answer/id #uuid "8d9403b5-aafb-5d53-aa6d-0e5daf290a1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\theta +2)^{3}(7.7)^{-\\theta -3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b6284b9-9a9f-5ee1-920b-8bb95737b84a" :answer/id #uuid "9b6284b9-9a9f-5ee1-920b-8bb95737b84a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\theta +2)^{4}(6.1)^{-\\theta -3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-492a6c1b-401b-53e4-ba39-5675e2455008" :answer/id #uuid "492a6c1b-401b-53e4-ba39-5675e2455008" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\theta +2)^{7.7}(3)^{-\\theta -3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186193201 :question/problem "Let ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},{X}_{3}$ be I.I.D. random variables with probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x;\\theta )=\\theta {x}^{-\\theta -1},\\,x\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\theta $ is an unknown parameter. Find the likelihood function of the sample $2.1,\\,3.2,\\,5.0.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ are independent and identically distributed continuous random variables with probability density function $f(x;\\theta ),$ where $\\theta $ is an unknown parameter, then the likelihood function of a random sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is\n\n$$\nL(\\theta )=P({X}_{1}={x}_{1},{X}_{2}={x}_{2},…,{X}_{n}={x}_{n})={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i};\\,\\theta ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we are given a sample of $n=3$ independent random variables with unknown parameter $\\theta ,$ for which the probability density function is\n\n$$\nf(x;\\theta )=\\theta {x}^{-\\theta -1},\\,x\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the likelihood function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & ={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}(\\theta {x}_{i}^{-\\theta -1}) \\\\  & ={\\theta }^{n}\\cdot {\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{-\\theta -1} \\\\  & ={\\theta }^{n}({\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})^{-\\theta -1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor our sample, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} & =2.1\\cdot 3.2\\cdot 5.0=33.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand $n=3.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nL(\\theta )={\\theta }^{3}(33.6)^{-\\theta -1}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186191092 :answer-field/correct "answer-6fe4d4c8-7b74-55c2-8864-41564a86d11f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-817339c5-e032-5434-8fb9-211e26758437" "answer-5548e192-7fc1-5720-a683-fb26a4860eb2" "answer-b25835e4-1079-513b-ba55-ed11d841865a" "answer-6fe4d4c8-7b74-55c2-8864-41564a86d11f" "answer-9f13f3b0-8682-52a7-a266-73a7860826f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-817339c5-e032-5434-8fb9-211e26758437" :answer/id #uuid "817339c5-e032-5434-8fb9-211e26758437" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\theta }^{33.6}(3)^{-\\theta -1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5548e192-7fc1-5720-a683-fb26a4860eb2" :answer/id #uuid "5548e192-7fc1-5720-a683-fb26a4860eb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\theta }^{33.6}(4)^{-\\theta -1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b25835e4-1079-513b-ba55-ed11d841865a" :answer/id #uuid "b25835e4-1079-513b-ba55-ed11d841865a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\theta }^{33.6}(4)^{-\\theta }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fe4d4c8-7b74-55c2-8864-41564a86d11f" :answer/id #uuid "6fe4d4c8-7b74-55c2-8864-41564a86d11f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\theta }^{3}(33.6)^{-\\theta -1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f13f3b0-8682-52a7-a266-73a7860826f0" :answer/id #uuid "9f13f3b0-8682-52a7-a266-73a7860826f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\theta }^{4}(33.6)^{-\\theta }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cb9c4cb7-5063-5801-b2b1-37e6379336d1" :question/id #uuid "cb9c4cb7-5063-5801-b2b1-37e6379336d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-159921" :question/problem "Let ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},{X}_{3}$ be I.I.D. random variables with probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x;\\theta )=(\\theta +1){x}^{-\\theta -2},\\,x\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\theta $ is an unknown parameter. Find the likelihood function of the sample $1.2,\\,1.5,\\,2.5.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ are independent and identically distributed continuous random variables with probability density function $f(x;\\theta ),$ where $\\theta $ is an unknown parameter, then the likelihood function of a random sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is\n\n$$\nL(\\theta )=P({X}_{1}={x}_{1},{X}_{2}={x}_{2},…,{X}_{n}={x}_{n})={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i};\\,\\theta ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we are given a sample of $n=3$ independent random variables with unknown parameter $\\theta ,$ for which the probability density function is\n\n$$\nf(x;\\theta )=(\\theta +1){x}^{-\\theta -2},\\,x\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the likelihood function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & ={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}((\\theta +1){x}_{i}^{-\\theta -2}) \\\\  & =(\\theta +1)^{n}\\cdot {\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{-\\theta -2} \\\\  & =(\\theta +1)^{n}({\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})^{-\\theta -2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor our sample, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} & =1.2\\cdot 1.5\\cdot 2.5=4.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand $n=3.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nL(\\theta )=(\\theta +1)^{3}(4.5)^{-\\theta -2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cf45163a-b1a9-5557-a7de-57f1ef3770a0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cf45163a-b1a9-5557-a7de-57f1ef3770a0" :answer-field/id #uuid "cf45163a-b1a9-5557-a7de-57f1ef3770a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-76830c10-9f47-5b30-